# CallScope - project context

A live voice agent (Hermes Agent = reasoning backend) plus an evaluation harness, call-review
workflow, model-improvement loop and governance artifacts. **Runtime:** local demo on Apple Silicon
(Mac); ASR/VAD/TTS native; agent LLM via Nebius Token Factory (optional local LLM fallback).
Showcase = `make demo` + video + static site (not a public GPU VM). Design of record:
`docs/design/CallScope_Phase3_Design.md`. Read the relevant section before implementing.

## Stack
Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy 2 + Alembic, Postgres 16, optional MinIO/local disk,
LiveKit + LiveKit Agents (native `livekit-server`), Hermes Agent (API server + `hermes-callscope`
plugin), Token Factory OpenAI-compatible LLM, native ASR/TTS (MLX/ONNX candidates),
Prometheus/Grafana, MLflow, Streamlit (review console), TypeScript static web client. Tooling: uv,
ruff, mypy (strict), pytest, pre-commit, GitHub Actions, Docker Compose (data plane only).

## Layout
`callscope/` shared library (events, providers, norm, eval, datasets, governance, observability,
devtools) | `apps/{api,worker,biz,review,web}` | `servers/{asr,tts}` |
`plugins/hermes_callscope` | `eval/{scenarios,thresholds.yaml,baselines,cassettes}` | `infra/` |
`db/schema.sql` + `migrations/` | `docs/` | `backlog/tasks.yaml` | `prompts/`.

## Ground rules
1. Work is driven by tasks in `backlog/tasks.yaml`. Follow `20-workflow-artifacts.mdc` for every task.
2. Never invent API details of Hermes, LiveKit, Token Factory or model libraries. Check installed
   package source/docs; if unsure, say so and write a spike note in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.
3. The voice worker is the latency source of truth (ADR-006). Measure with a monotonic clock.
4. Providers (STT/TTS/Brain) always sit behind the interfaces in `callscope/providers/base.py`.
5. Small, reviewable changes: one task per branch, one PR per task.
6. If a task conflicts with the design doc, stop and propose a decision-log entry instead of
   silently deviating.
7. LLM spend is budget-capped; CI uses cassettes only; live Token Factory calls need `--live`.
